 "minimum_revision_contract": {
  "rule": "Add an implementation-independent capability that selected-language material may select designated UI image variants, with missing translation retaining the original image identity. Point the controls key diagrams and representative battle/UI images to that rule; include one original-resource and one translated-resource input/output vector. Keep media existence and load failures in resource contracts, and avoid requiring source paths, Ruby APIs or an architecture.",
  "preserve_correct_scope": [
   "Not all image resources are translated; e.g. the controls backdrop is not wrapped by the translation service.",
   "All 18 catalog domains retain their identities; resource strings are still SCRIPT_TEXTS entries.",
   "No actual media presence, image rendering, reachable controls menu or language switch has been run.",
   "No guarantee that a bad translated filename falls back to the original image.",
   "No reference or framework implementation changes."
  ],
